 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Performance:** On the Blender dataset, the hybrid strategy achieves a PSNR of 30.3 dB, SSIM of 0.945, and LPIPS of 0.078 [S1].
-*   **Comparison:** Removing the hybrid strategy ('w/o hybrid') reduces PSNR to 26.6 dB, SSIM to 0.925, and increases LPIPS to 0.163 [S1]. This demonstrates that the hybrid strategy yields better rendering quality than single-stage training [S1].
-*   **Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
-*   **Strengths:** Improves view synthesis performance by jointly using spherical harmonics, the coarse-to-fine strategy, and a consistency filter function [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Not given in the sources.
+*   **Performance:** The hybrid strategy yields better rendering quality than single-stage training [S1].
+*   **Metrics:** On the Blender dataset, the full method achieves PSNR 30.3 dB, SSIM 0.945, and LPIPS 0.078 [S1].
+*   **Comparison:** Removing the strategy ("w/o hybrid") degrades performance to PSNR 26.6 dB, SSIM 0.925, and LPIPS 0.163 [S1].
+*   **Strengths:** Improved view synthesis performance, stable convergence, better handling of complex geometries.
+*   **Limitations:** Requires multiple training stages, potentially increasing total training time compared to a single-stage approach.
